@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] guest-telemetry-untrusted
Guest OTLP payloads MUST NOT assign outer host, VM, placement or execution
identity. The receiver MUST replace resource identity from Audi's Lilly-derived
binding and MUST NOT forward arbitrary attributes, events, links or log records.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity] guest-telemetry-bounded
The receiver MUST bound each body, protobuf object count and concurrent request.
It MUST accept only a fixed metric name vocabulary and enforce per-VM and
host-wide request/byte budgets so guests cannot create unbounded series or
trace volume across repeated accepted requests.
An invalid or oversized request MUST NOT reach the local collector. Receiver
failure MUST NOT stop Audi, Lilly or guest execution.
